WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.536
Part eleven.

00:00:01.536 --> 00:00:02.955
API tests.

00:00:04.833 --> 00:00:07.652
The Demo Books mobile app talks to an API.

00:00:07.652 --> 00:00:11.536
You can test it right in Pocket QA, next to your UI scenarios.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.541
Open API Tests from the Tools tab.

00:00:14.967 --> 00:00:18.508
Requests live in folders, here Demo Books API.

00:00:18.508 --> 00:00:23.537
The environment up top holds the server address, used through a baseUrl variable.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.449
The Sign in request posts an email and a password in its body.

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:37.811
Its Save values tab takes the token from the reply and keeps it in a token variable.

00:00:37.833 --> 00:00:41.597
Click Send: it passes, and the token is saved.

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:51.517
The folder sends that token as a Bearer header with every request inside, so there is nothing to paste.

00:00:55.733 --> 00:00:58.901
So My account just works, and gets Anna's account back.

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:09.011
For List books, click a key in the JSON reply to turn it into a check.

00:01:10.867 --> 00:01:14.672
The new check lands in the Checks tab, and passes on the next send.

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:22.308
Run folder sends every request in turn, each one marked pass or fail.

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:31.280
A failure says what was expected and what came back: a price of 20 expected, 18 returned.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:35.309
Export to Postman to run with Newman in CI.

00:01:35.533 --> 00:01:42.131
The other way, Paste cURL makes a request from a curl command, and Import takes a Postman collection.

00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:45.573
Finally, let's look at the settings you only set once.
